***************************************************************************************
    Beam Normalization Error Calculator
			Version 2.2
				2010/12/14 H.Kubo
***************************************************************************************

1. Initialization
	  HadErrCalc *HEC = new HadErrCalc("your_installed_path/share/");

	it takes several seconds to read error contribution histograms.

	note: please do NOT create many HadErrCalc objects.
              it uses about 20MB of memoly per object.
	
2. Calculation
   2.1 Set Input Histograms

	Inputs are histogram pointers of NSK(#of event at SK) & NND (#of event at ND)
	with 50 MeV x 200bin (0-10 GeV) for 3 neutrino flavors.
	Oscillation params. and systematic terms other than beam should be treated in your side.	
	
	ND histograms are always required.
	
	 HEC->SetNDHist(hnd_numu, hnd_numub, hnd_nue);

	SK histograms are optional, if you set only 1Rmu histograms
	Calculator does not calculate Nue errors.
	(returns 0 for nue errors, and will be faster by factor 3!!)
	
	 HEC->Set1RmuHist(h1rmu_numu, h1rmu_numub, h1rmu_nue);
	 HEC->SetNueSigHist(hsig_nue); // only 1 input for Nue Signal
         HEC->SetNueBGHist(hbkg_numu, hbkg_numub, hbkg_nue);

    2.2 Calculation
	 just 1 command.
	   HEC->Calc();
	 then, results are stored.

    2.3 Get Results
	 Outputs are all fractional 1sigma errors.
	
            HEC->GetSumErr(0);  // fractional error of 1Rmu/ND
	    HEC->GetSumErr(1);  // fractional error of NueSig/ND
	    HEC->GetSumErr(2);  // fractional error of NueBG/ND
	    HEC->GetSumErr(3);  // fractional error of (NueSig+NueBG)/ND

	 NueSig+NueBG error is similar but slightly smaller than
	 { ( NueSig error ) * NueSig + ( NueBG error) * NueBG }/(NueSig + NueBG)
	 due to Signal:BG correlation.
	 
	 you can also get flavor by flavor fractional errors by GetErr(),
	 NSK errors by GetSKErr(), and NND errors by GetNDErr()
	
    2.4 Loop 2.1~2.3 with different histograms (with different osc. parameters)

	 note: Even if the pointes of histograms are the same,
	       you should set histograms again.
	       Because, histogram contents are copied to c++ array and used in order to
	       avoid function overhead from huge number of calls of TH1::GetBinContent().


please see and try "test.cc" as a more practical example.

History:
   2010/12/01 v1.0 : first release
   2010/12/09 v2.0 : error tables are updated with jnubeam 10d-tune v.2 MC.
   2010/12/11 v2.1 : beam Off-axis angle error 1.0mrad -> 0.4mrad
   2010/12/14 v2.2 : beam Off-axis angle error 1.0mrad -> 0.44mrad
